T1.4  Database layer and initial migration
Date: 2026-11-21
Commands run:
  uv run pytest backend/tests/test_db.py backend/tests/test_migrations.py -> 19 passed
  ACCOUNTABLE_DB=<temp>/a.db uv run --directory backend alembic upgrade head; then alembic current
    -> "0001_initial (head)"
Design notes:
  - Five tables in Core with every spec 6.1 constraint as a named CHECK or FK, and the spec 6.2 indexes
    (the stage_changes.deal_id FK is covered by ix_stage_changes_deal_id_changed_at, which leads with it).
  - The connection hook (E-1) runs the four PRAGMAs in autocommit mode, then switches Python 3.12's sqlite3 to
    autocommit=False, so every statement, DDL included, runs inside a transaction. That's what makes a failed
    migration roll back completely without any other text SQL (no "BEGIN" statement).
  - Migration 0001 is written out in full (not imported from db.py); a test checks it matches db.metadata.
  - Start-up (main.run): port check, then upgrade_to_head, then the start-up log lines. A damaged file stops
    start-up with one line and is left byte-for-byte unchanged.
Tests: settings read back (foreign_keys 1, wal, synchronous 2 = FULL, busy_timeout 5000); bad status, stage, value,
  probability and organization refused by the database; one-parent check; R31-R33 FK behaviour on the rows;
  indexes; rollback; a source scan showing the PRAGMAs in the hook are the only text SQL (V-B02, E-1);
  empty -> head, re-run is a no-op, migration = metadata, a failure half way leaves no tables, a damaged
  file is unchanged (V-B13 part).
Files changed: backend/app/db.py, backend/alembic.ini, backend/migrations/env.py, script.py.mako,
  versions/0001_initial.py, backend/app/main.py (start-up migrate), backend/tests/test_db.py, test_migrations.py
Requirements covered: spec 6.1-6.3, REL-1, REL-2, REL-9, ADR-004, DEP-4, E-1, ENG-4, SEC-5
Open issues: V-B13 "from the previous version with data" needs a second migration, and is added then.

