Engineer decision (Phase 4): e2e clocks
Date: 2026-11-21
Question raised at the start of Phase 4 (open issue from C3): the e2e browser clock is fixed at
  2026-11-21 14:30 (e2e/fixtures.ts) but the e2e backend used the computer's clock, so date-dependent
  assertions would fail on any other day. Options: (a) a test-only fixed clock for the backend, or
  (b) stop fixing the browser clock.
Decision: (a), "Fixed backend clock (Recommended)", chosen by the engineer and relayed by the Phase 3 session.
Change:
  - backend/app/config.py: load_settings() reads ACCOUNTABLE_FIXED_NOW (a local ISO date and time, no time zone);
    when set, the clock is FixedClock at that moment, otherwise SystemClock as before. A bad value stops with a
    ConfigError naming the variable.
  - backend/app/main.py: start-up logs a WARNING "clock fixed at ... by ACCOUNTABLE_FIXED_NOW (tests only)" when it
    is set, so it can't be on unnoticed.
  - scripts/run-tests.mjs: sets ACCOUNTABLE_FIXED_NOW=2026-11-21T14:30:00 for the e2e and perf suites only (pytest
    fixes its own clock). playwright.config.ts passes it to the backend server. Since the seed/clear commands in
    fixtures.ts inherit the same environment, the sample data is seeded relative to the same moment.
  - e2e/fixtures.ts: refuses to run unless ACCOUNTABLE_FIXED_NOW equals FIXED_NOW, so the two can't drift.
  - backend/tests/test_config.py (new): unset gives SystemClock; set gives that now and today; three bad values
    are refused.
  npm run dev never sets it: package.json's dev script and scripts/ensure-installed.mjs are unchanged, so users
  always get the computer's clock. DEP-2's documented variables are unchanged; this one is test-only.
Commands run: uv run pytest backend/tests/test_config.py backend/tests/test_security.py backend/tests/test_cli.py
  -> 63 passed. The full npm test with it is recorded under Checkpoint C4.

