  6 passed. No console errors in either mode.
  The donut has no tooltip by design (its values are listed beside it).
Findings and fixes (each a token change, no dark-only rule):
  1. Field outlines, the dashed "Add deal" buttons and the drop gap used --sea-mist (a fill) as a line:
     too bright on black. New --line: #cdd8db in light (unchanged), #527280 in dark (4.1:1 on the panel,
     3.2:1 on the page). tokens.test.ts checks it's at least 3:1 in dark.
  2. Row menus, the side panel, the delete dialog, chart tooltips and a lifted card were black on black, so
     they lost their edges (shadows don't show on black). New --raised: #ffffff in light (unchanged),
     #0e3240 in dark (1.55:1 against black; every text color 5.1:1 or more on it, now in tokens.test.ts).
  3. The toggle, a black secondary button on the black top bar, had no visible edge. Secondary buttons now
     use --raised too (white in light, unchanged).
  4. The toggle showed no focus ring. Cause, which predates this change: :focus-visible's ring and
     .btn-secondary's shadow have the same specificity, and the shadow comes later in global.css, so no
     secondary button shows a ring, in either mode. Fixed for the toggle (.theme-toggle:focus-visible keeps
     both). Fixing every secondary button changes light mode's focused look (R94), so it's recorded in spec
     17.1 for the product owner to decide.
  5. The toggle's icon went from 16px to 18px, to sit better next to Add deal's "+".
