dark-mode T7 (continued)  Focus ring on every secondary button
Date: 2026-11-26
The product owner asked for the secondary-button focus gap (spec 17.1) to be fixed, accepting the light-mode
  change to the focused look.
Checked first: which focusable elements set their own box-shadow. Only .btn-secondary. Pipeline cards and
  closed rows have a shadow, but the focusable element is their .draggable wrapper, which has none; the search
  box shows its ring with :focus-within; menu items show focus as a highlighted row.
Fix: frontend/src/styles/global.css - .btn-secondary:focus-visible { box-shadow: var(--shadow), var(--focus-ring) },
  replacing the toggle-only rule.
Why it went unnoticed: V-E11's focused() counted any box-shadow as a focus indicator, and a secondary button's
  soft shadow passed. Tightened (e2e/keyboard.spec.ts): visible only with an outline, a box-shadow holding the
  --focus-ring color (read from the page, so either mode), a .search wrapper with the ring, a highlighted
  menu item, or Chrome's calendar button inside a date field. New test: in both modes, Tab reaches the toggle
  and the deals table's "Next" (45 deals, so it's enabled) with every stop showing focus.
Runs:
  First run of the tightened V-E11 -> 2 failed, 2 passed.
    - The new test aimed at the organizations table's "Next", which is disabled (12 organizations, one page)
      and can't take focus. Moved to the deals table.
    - The deal-by-keyboard test flagged input "Close date". A probe showed that after typing a date, Tab
      moves focus to Chrome's own calendar button inside the field: the input stays document.activeElement
      but no longer matches :focus. A close-up screenshot shows Chrome's own outline on the button, so focus
      is visible. The check now allows that case (date, datetime-local and time inputs not matching :focus).
  Rerun -> 4 passed.
  Probe: the .btn-secondary:focus-visible rule removed -> 4 failed (each at the toggle, its first secondary
    button); restored (grep finds the rule once).
  Light-mode comparison -> 1 failed: the delete dialog, 504 pixels. The diff shows only the ring around
    Cancel, which the dialog focuses when it opens: the approved change. The comparison now puts back the
    old shadow on .btn-secondary:focus-visible (style tag, like the toggle), so every other pixel is still
    compared exactly. Rerun -> 8 passed.
Docs: spec R94 (the approved exception), 3.9 Buttons, the toggle bullet, V-E11, and 17.1 (gap removed);
  plan files table, phase 8 and Proof; docs/STATUS.md.
Requirements covered: NFR-7 (focus visible on every secondary button, both modes), R94.
Harness note: V-E11 counted any box-shadow as a focus indicator, so secondary buttons without a ring passed - caught by the phase 5 walkthrough (by eye) - V-E11 now requires the ring color, and a probe without the fix fails all four tests.
